 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk county to establish a special medical district and to appropriate, collect and expend monies in furtherance thereof",
    "basePrintNo": "S5950",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5950-2009",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5950\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk county to establish\na special medical district and to appropriate, collect and expend\nmonies in furtherance thereof\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis legislation would authorize the establishment of a special\nmedical district in the unincorporated Fire Island Pines area of the\ntown of Brookhaven.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of this bill is a special act to authorize the Town of\nBrookhaven, under the procedural special improvement district\nestablishment provisions set forth in Article 12-A of the Town Law, to\nestablish a medical district in the unincorporated Fire Island Pines\narea of the Town of Brookhaven, Suffolk County. This special medical\ndistrict is needed to allow Fire Island Pines to contract for EMS\nservices, provide housing for EMTs among other necessary medical\nservices.  Section 2 allows the town board certain authorities as it\npertains to acquire, build and maintain real property or structure.\nSection 3 states that costs and expenses approved by this act shall be\nassessed, levied, and collected from the lots and parcels located\nwithin the unincorporated Fire Island pines area.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nFire Island Pines is a summer community with public beaches and a\nlarge public transient dock facility located on Fire Island. The only\naccess to this area is by ferry or private boat. A helicopter is used\nin cases of a medical emergency. The property owners in the Fire\nIsland Pines area are interested in establishing a special medical\ndistrict to ensure that Emergency Medical Services are readily\navailable. All attendant costs would spread throughout the community.\nSuch special medical districts as this have been established elsewhere\nthroughout the State, including Davis Park on Fire Island in 1988.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
