    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S5950A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\nAn act authorizing the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk county to establish\na special improvement district or benefited area for medical services\nand to appropriate, collect and expend monies in furtherance thereof\n\n\n PURPOSE :\nThis legislation would authorize the establishment of a special\nimprovement district for medical services in the unincorporated Fire\nIsland pines area of the town of Brookhaven.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\nSection 1 of this bill allows the town board of the town of Brookhaven\nto establish a special improvement district to establish and equip a\nsuitable building for a medical facility for the unincorporated Fire\nIsland pines area of the town of Brookhaven.  Section 2 authorizes the\ntown board to appropriate, collect and expend sums deemed necessary to\nreconstruct, repair, operate, equip, and maintain a suitable building\nand to acquire any necessary real property.\n\nSection 3 States that costs shall be assessed, levied and collected\nfrom the several lots and parcels of land within the special\nimprovement district.\n\nSection 4 is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\nFire Island pines is a summer community with public beaches and a\nlarge public transient dock facility located on Fire Island. The only\naccess to this area is by ferry or private boat. A helicopter is used\nin cases of a medical emergency. The property owners in the Fire\nIsland pines area are interested in establishing a special improvement\ndistrict to ensure that Emergency Medical Services are readily\navailable. All attendant costs would spread throughout the community.\nSuch special improvement districts as this have been established\nelsewhere throughout the State, including Davis park on Fire Island in\n1988.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
