    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Towns",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5950B\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\nAn act authorizing the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk county to establish a\nspecial improvement district for a medical facility for the Fire Island\nPines area of the town of Brookhaven\n\nPURPOSE:\nThis legislation would authorize the establishment of a special improve-\nment district in the unincorporated Fire Island Pines area of the town\nof Brookhaven.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\nSection 1 of this bill is a special act to authorize the town board of\nthe Town of Brookhaven to establish a special improvement district\npursuant to article 12 or 12-A of the town law, to construct, recon-\nstruct, repair, operate, equip and maintain a suitable building for a\nmedical facility for the population of the unincorporated Fire Island\nPines area of the town of Brookhaven, Suffolk county, New York, and to\nacquire by purchase, lease or gift necessary lands therefor. Notwith-\nstanding the provisions of any law to the contrary, the town board of\nthe town of Brookhaven may contract with a medical entity for the\nprovision of emergency medical services to promote the health, safety\nand welfare of the residents and visitors of the Fire Island Pines area.\nThe town board is authorized and empowered to appropriate the sums\nrequired to be paid under the terms of such contract.\n\nSection 2 allows the town board certain authorities as it pertains to\nacquiring, building and maintaining real property or structure.\n\nSection 3 states that costs and expenses approved by this act shall be\nassessed, levied, and collected from the lots and parcels located within\nthe unincorporated Fire Island Pines area.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\nFire Island Pines is a summer community with public beaches and a large\npublic transient dock facility located on Fire Island. The only access\nto this area is by ferry or private boat. A helicopter is used in cases\nof a medical emergency. The property owners in the Fire Island Pines\narea are interested in establishing a special improvement district to\nensure that Emergency Medical Services are readily available. All\nattendant costs would spread throughout the community. Such special\nimprovement districts as this have been established elsewhere throughout\nthe State, including Davis Park on Fire Island in 1990.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\nNew Bill.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\nNone.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n\n",
